{"is_error":false,"duration_api_ms":55778,"num_turns":1,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"2574b84c-57b0-4197-b23f-422aaffe7578","total_cost_usd":0.3669655,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":23424,"cache_read_input_tokens":20135,"output_tokens":4375,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":23424,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":4375,"cache_read_input_tokens":20135,"cache_creation_input_tokens":23424,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":23424},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":13178,"outputTokens":19,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.013273,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000,"canonicalModel":"claude-haiku-4-5","provider":"firstParty"},"claude-opus-5":{"inputTokens":2,"outputTokens":4375,"cacheReadInputTokens":20135,"cacheCreationInputTokens":23424,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.3536925,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"canonicalModel":"claude-opus-5","provider":"firstParty"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\"agent\":\"lore-critic\",\"verdict\":\"revise\",\"summary\":\"Most items sit correctly on the sprite readings and the table, but several assert value or altitude claims the passages do not support, one invents a payout inference, and two items carry the wrong size or fragility read against the loot table.\",\"reviews\":[{\"id\":\"torn_foil_blanket\",\"verdict\":\"revise\",\"issues\":[{\"type\":\"number_disagrees\",\"quote\":\"Lightest thing on the tether and worth about what that suggests down here.\",\"evidence\":\"torn_foil_blanket 15 kg — the lightest row in the loot table is torn_foil_blanket at 15 kg, but [2.6a] \\\"Value scales with mass on top of the altitude gradient\\\"\",\"cites\":[\"2.6a\"],\"why\":\"The superlative on mass is supported by the table, but \\\"worth about what that suggests\\\" folds mass straight into a price the writer states as fact; value in the passages is a multiplier on altitude with mass on top, not a figure the piece announces about itself. The lightest-row claim can stay; the payout gloss cannot.\"}],\"corrected\":{\"flavour\":\"A flat grey hexagon of skin plate, split corner to corner and chipped out of one edge, still holding a bevelled shine along the top. Fifteen kilos — the lightest thing you will ever hang off the tether.\"}},{\"id\":\"crumpled_panel_stack\",\"verdict\":\"revise\",\"issues\":[{\"type\":\"invented_mechanic\",\"quote\":\"cheap enough that the fuel to fetch it is the real cost\",\"evidence\":\"[2.6a] \\\"a ballistic arc never pays for circularisation, which is most of the delta-v ... circularising costs the rest of the tank and buys time.\\\"\",\"cites\":[\"2.6a\"],\"why\":\"The passages describe fuel as a route decision for the whole trip, not a per-piece cost that can be weighed against one item's payout. Framing a single 24 kg piece as costing more fuel than it returns implies an accounting the game does not run.\"}],\"corrected\":{\"flavour\":\"Pale beige quilting laid over white, rust and blue under-sheets, with a ragged hole burnt clean through the top face. Twenty-four kilos of soft goods off the bottom of the band, where the multiplier starts at 1.0.\"}},{\"id\":\"cracked_solar_array\",\"verdict\":\"pass\",\"issues\":[]},{\"id\":\"bent_truss_section\",\"verdict\":\"pass\",\"issues\":[]},{\"id\":\"spent_kick_motor_casing\",\"verdict\":\"pass\",\"issues\":[]},{\"id\":\"collapsed_dish_frame\",\"verdict\":\"revise\",\"issues\":[{\"type\":\"contradicts_gdd\",\"quote\":\"the low band pays low\",\"evidence\":\"[2.6a] \\\"One continuous orbital band, 50,000 m to 280,000 m, with a value gradient — no tiers, no discrete altitudes to keep in sync.\\\" and [4.3] \\\"Discrete altitude bands. One continuous envelope with a value gradient does the same job with nothing to keep in sync (§2.6).\\\"\",\"cites\":[\"2.6a\",\"4.3\"],\"why\":\"\\\"The low band\\\" names a discrete band, which §4.3 records as cut from scope. There is one band; what varies inside it is a continuous multiplier.\"}],\"corrected\":{\"flavour\":\"A shallow grey dish still bolted to its little trapezoid stand, feed arm reaching to a brass knob over the centre, rim dented and split down one side. Eighty-two kilos of awkward, and this low down the multiplier is barely off the floor.\"}},{\"id\":\"shredded_antenna_mesh\",\"verdict\":\"pass\",\"issues\":[]},{\"id\":\"cracked_battery_pallet\",\"verdict\":\"pass\",\"issues\":[]},{\"id\":\"burst_pressurant_sphere\",\"verdict\":\"pass\",\"issues\":[]},{\"id\":\"delaminated_radiator_fin\",\"verdict\":\"pass\",\"issues\":[]},{\"id\":\"torn_solar_wing_spar\",\"verdict\":\"revise\",\"issues\":[{\"type\":\"number_disagrees\",\"quote\":\"Middle of the envelope, middle of the money.\",\"evidence\":\"[2.6a] \\\"a piece's value multiplier interpolates on its altitude from 1.0 at the floor to 5.5 at the ceiling\\\" — torn_solar_wing_spar sits at 131,000 m in a 50,000–280,000 m envelope, which is 35% of the way up, not the middle.\",\"cites\":[\"2.6a\"],\"why\":\"131,000 m is barely a third of the way through the 50,000–280,000 m envelope. The size-class label \\\"middle third\\\" is a bucket in the table, not a position in the envelope, and the line reads the bucket as the midpoint.\"}],\"corrected\":{\"flavour\":\"Two tall panels side by side, each ruled into dark blue cells behind pale dividers, the right one hanging a few degrees out of true. A third of the way up the envelope, where the multiplier has only just started to climb.\"}},{\"id\":\"cracked_optics_barrel\",\"verdict\":\"pass\",\"issues\":[]},{\"id\":\"fractured_docking_collar\",\"verdict\":\"pass\",\"issues\":[]},{\"id\":\"dead_thruster_quad\",\"verdict\":\"pass\",\"issues\":[]},{\"id\":\"buckled_pressure_bulkhead\",\"verdict\":\"revise\",\"issues\":[{\"type\":\"invented_mechanic\",\"quote\":\"Wide enough to fight the tether the whole way down.\",\"evidence\":\"[4.3] \\\"Size classes, fragile flag, compactor, crane magnet, oversized junk. All exist to serve the endgame. Every piece is one slot; the module is simply very heavy.\\\" and [2.6a] \\\"Value scales with mass on top of the altitude gradient, so the good stuff fights you on the tether\\\"\",\"cites\":[\"4.3\",\"2.6a\"],\"why\":\"§2.6 says mass is what fights you on the tether; §4.3 records size classes and oversized junk as cut, with every piece taking one slot. Attributing the tether fight to width rather than the 148 kg makes size a physical property the tether responds to.\"}],\"corrected\":{\"flavour\":\"A ragged-edged grey plate with a long crease folded through the middle and chips still shedding off one side. A hundred and forty-eight kilos, and every one of them pulls on the way down.\"}},{\"id\":\"ruptured_helium_tank\",\"verdict\":\"pass\",\"issues\":[]},{\"id\":\"shattered_star_tracker\",\"verdict\":\"pass\",\"issues\":[]},{\"id\":\"warped_gyro_deck\",\"verdict\":\"pass\",\"issues\":[]},{\"id\":\"cracked_ablative_nose_cone\",\"verdict\":\"pass\",\"issues\":[]},{\"id\":\"split_avionics_rack\",\"verdict\":\"pass\",\"issues\":[]},{\"id\":\"torn_reactor_shield_plate\",\"verdict\":\"revise\",\"issues\":[{\"type\":\"contradicts_gdd\",\"quote\":\"High shelf, and the gradient up here is where the money is.\",\"evidence\":\"[2.6a] \\\"no tiers, no discrete altitudes to keep in sync\\\" and [4.3] \\\"Discrete altitude bands. One continuous envelope with a value gradient does the same job\\\"\",\"cites\":[\"2.6a\",\"4.3\"],\"why\":\"\\\"High shelf\\\" is shelf language for a structure the document explicitly cut. The rest of the sentence is right — height is where the money is — but it must not sit on a shelf.\"}],\"corrected\":{\"flavour\":\"A jagged green shard with two yellow stripes and a couple of surviving chips, a splinter floating free beside it and a curled rust-brown wire trailing below. Fell from two hundred and nine thousand metres, and that is most of what it is worth.\"}},{\"id\":\"cracked_deep_space_dish\",\"verdict\":\"revise\",\"issues\":[{\"type\":\"number_disagrees\",\"quote\":\"Bulky, high, and dear\",\"evidence\":\"cracked_deep_space_dish — 78 kg | medium. The table's oversized rows are collapsed_dish_frame (82 kg), buckled_pressure_bulkhead (148 kg) and severed_boom_mast (165 kg).\",\"cites\":[\"2.6a\"],\"why\":\"At 78 kg and size class medium this is the lightest piece in the whole top third; \\\"bulky\\\" reads it as one of the oversized rows it is not.\"}],\"corrected\":{\"flavour\":\"A grey parabola on a blocky base, feed arm strutted across its face, rim buckled irregular all round. Light for how high it fell from, and it will crack if you land it hard.\"}},{\"id\":\"fused_ion_grid_assembly\",\"verdict\":\"pass\",\"issues\":[]},{\"id\":\"severed_boom_mast\",\"verdict\":\"pass\",\"issues\":[]},{\"id\":\"scorched_fuel_cell_stack\",\"verdict\":\"pass\",\"issues\":[]},{\"id\":\"shattered_cryo_dewar\",\"verdict\":\"revise\",\"issues\":[{\"type\":\"wrong_voice\",\"quote\":\"Not a scratch on it, which is exactly why it will not take one.\",\"evidence\":\"[1c] \\\"Armstrong narrates over the radio — a dozen state-triggered one-liners (\\\\\\\"Chute stays packed while she's glowing, kid\\\\\\\")\\\"\",\"cites\":[\"1c\"],\"why\":\"The epigram turns on itself for the shape of the sentence rather than telling the player anything. The register here is a junkyard hand naming what will go wrong, not a paradox.\"}],\"corrected\":{\"flavour\":\"A bright cyan rounded tank on its side, stub fittings at both ends, a nozzle on top and H2O stencilled in black across the middle. Came through everything whole so far, and it is on you to keep it that way.\"}},{\"id\":\"impact_pitted_engine_bell\",\"verdict\":\"revise\",\"issues\":[{\"type\":\"contradicts_gdd\",\"quote\":\"from the dear end of the band\",\"evidence\":\"[2.6a] \\\"a piece's value multiplier interpolates on its altitude from 1.0 at the floor to 5.5 at the ceiling\\\" — impact_pitted_engine_bell sits at 259,500 m, near the ceiling.\",\"cites\":[\"2.6a\"],\"why\":\"\\\"End of the band\\\" is close, but the band is continuous and the ceiling is where the 5.5 sits — the piece is near the top of a gradient, not at a dear end of a range. Minor, and the fix is one phrase.\"}],\"corrected\":{\"flavour\":\"A flared cone standing on ring ridges, throat blacked with soot and the base rim crusted rust-brown. A hundred and twenty-two kilos of dense metal from near the top of the envelope, where the multiplier is close to its best.\"}},{\"id\":\"cracked_command_module_hatch\",\"verdict\":\"revise\",\"issues\":[{\"type\":\"invented_mechanic\",\"quote\":\"Absurd that a fastener pays this well, but it fell from that high.\",\"evidence\":\"[2.6a] \\\"a piece's value multiplier interpolates on its altitude from 1.0 at the floor to 5.5 at the ceiling ... Value scales with mass on top of the altitude gradient\\\"\",\"cites\":[\"2.6a\"],\"why\":\"The line has the piece comment on its own payout as a surprise, which requires the writer to know what the player is paid and to judge it against an expectation the game never sets. The altitude fact is fine; the appraisal is not.\"}],\"corrected\":{\"flavour\":\"One six-sided ring, face-on, hole through the middle, a highlight on the upper left and nothing else in the frame. A hundred and twelve kilos of it, though, and it came down from two hundred and sixty-eight thousand metres.\"}},{\"id\":\"armstrongs_module\",\"verdict\":\"revise\",\"issues\":[{\"type\":\"number_disagrees\",\"quote\":\"it will take the whole tank to bring it home\",\"evidence\":\"[2.6a] \\\"a ballistic arc never pays for circularisation, which is most of the delta-v ... circularising costs the rest of the tank and buys time. Both are legal at every altitude\\\"\",\"cites\":[\"2.6a\"],\"why\":\"The tank is spent on the route decision — ballistic versus circularised — and §2.6 says both are legal at every altitude. Asserting that this piece consumes the whole tank states a fuel cost the passages assign to the climb, not to the cargo.\"},{\"type\":\"contradicts_gdd\",\"quote\":\"dented at one corner where the years finally caught it\",\"evidence\":\"[5d] \\\"Satellite → Apollo-era module that degrades (pristine → damaged → scrap) instead of being destroyed, and its condition selects the ending and scales payout.\\\"\",\"cites\":[\"5d\"],\"why\":\"The module has three named conditions and the one the player finds is pristine; baking a dent into the flavour text describes it as already damaged, which is a state the game selects, not a fixed fact. The sprite reading does show the dent, so the description is grounded — but it must not be narrated as history that already happened to it.\"}],\"corrected\":{\"display_name\":\"Armstrong's Module\",\"flavour\":\"A grey canister banded twice in yellow, rimmed at both ends, one end dented and a chip broken off beside it. Apollo-era hardware that predates the cascade and outlived it, three and a half tonnes of it, hanging at the very top of the envelope.\"}}]}","ttft_ms":54563,"ttft_stream_ms":1380,"time_to_request_ms":213,"type":"result","duration_ms":54601,"uuid":"41b93b4e-b382-48ef-9902-ad7f1a08560e"}
